Hasho Stories Privacy Policy
Updated: October 14, 2026

This policy applies to the Hasho Stories / Hasho Storytelling mobile app published by Yusha (iOS bundle com.yusha.storytelling and Android package ai.hasho.storytelling). It describes this app rather than other Yusha apps or websites.

Local story and learning data
The app stores drawings, imported character images, built characters, saved adventures, language preferences, learning progress, friend personalization and conversation reports in its private storage on your device. These records support the stories, drawing activities, local personalization and progress reports. The app does not upload this content to an advertising network or a cloud AI service.

Microphone and image processing
Microphone access is requested for reading practice and character conversations. The release app processes speech on-device, using available on-device speech recognition or bundled local models. Microphone audio is not uploaded or saved as a recording by the release app. Text recognition results may be included in local progress and conversation reports. Drawings, photo imports, character reconstruction and character joint detection are processed on-device. Camera or photo-library access, when used, serves the user-selected image import feature.

Advertising and tracking
The app contains no advertising SDK, displays no third-party advertisements and does not collect an advertising identifier. It does not use Google Analytics, Firebase Analytics, advertising cookies or cross-app advertising tracking.

Existing account and subscription services
No sign-in is required to use the story and drawing activities. The app retains support for previously authenticated accounts and existing subscription records. Where such an account or purchase is present, our Supabase-hosted backend processes the account identifier, authentication/session information and, where applicable, store receipt or transaction information to maintain the account and verify paid access. Supabase acts as our hosting and database provider. The configured project is hosted in AWS region ap-northeast-1. These service communications also expose normal connection information, such as an IP address, to the hosting infrastructure. Apple or Google processes any store transaction under its own store terms. Story drawings, microphone recordings, local learning records and local conversation reports are not sent to this backend.

Analytics
The corrected release does not send product-use analytics for either guest or verified-account sessions. Local learning progress is retained only to support the activities and progress reports on the device. The app has no third-party analytics SDK.

Storage and choices
You can delete saved adventures through the app's visible deletion flow. Local app data remains in the device's private app storage until deleted or the app is removed; any operating-system backup is controlled by your device's backup settings. Existing server-side account or transaction records are separate from local story files. To request access to or deletion of those records, contact us at yusha@yusha.ai. We may retain records required to maintain an account, verify a purchase or meet applicable recordkeeping obligations.

Children's use
The story activities work without entering an email address or creating an account. The app does not request contact lists, precise location, advertising identifiers or information for advertising. Parents or guardians can contact us about a child's local or existing account data using the address below.

